I'm not entirely sure why you decided to accept the challenges if you
wanted to play pure-vanilla nethack, but I can understand that figuring
out how to ignore the challenges from the website might have been a bit
tough if you weren't exactly sure where the website was anyway.

I'd definitely agree that it would be nice if there were more in-game
information about turning off the challenges.  Help text or option
screen items, maybe?

I'm very much in favor of the challenges.  I really enjoy having to
deal with playing in a new way to get around a previously-unseen
constraint.  I have a pretty successful "standard" mechanism for
progressing through the dungeon; the challenges force me to confront
that and adopt new strategies.

Having said that, yeah, I found it initially frustrating to realize
that the Grue challenge didn't follow a turn count but rather something
more akin to a keystroke count.  Cost me at least two promising
characters.  But it was all the more satisfying to finally beat it as a
result, and it also led me to do some completely unorthodox things,
like using a random wish on a scroll of identify just so I could -- I
hoped -- complete it.  I could still definitely get behind the argument
that it should be turn-based (heck, the original grues were
replacements for bottomless pits, which didn't jump out at you if you
checked your inventory).

